# Packaging integrity only. This file changes no scientific content, no review
# verdict, no source inventory, and no governance status.
#
# MANIFEST.sha256 records SHA-256 over the raw bytes of this directory's Markdown
# files with LF line endings. Under Windows Git with core.autocrlf=true, a fresh
# checkout would otherwise rewrite those files with CRLF line endings, changing
# every byte count and invalidating every manifest entry even though no content
# changed. The rules below pin LF in the index and in the working tree so the
# manifest stays verifiable on every platform.
#
# This file is deliberately NOT listed in MANIFEST.sha256: the manifest contract
# covers every Markdown file in this directory and nothing else.

*.md            text eol=lf
MANIFEST.sha256 text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
